ARTICLE VII — ENFORCEMENT AND REMEDIES

The Sovereign reserves all remedies available at law and in equity,
including but not limited to:

  (a) Preliminary and permanent injunctive relief without bond;
  (b) Actual damages, including lost profits, reasonable royalties,
      and full disgorgement of unjust enrichment;
  (c) Statutory damages under applicable copyright law, including
      enhanced damages for willful infringement (up to $150,000 per work
      under 17 U.S.C. § 504(c)(2));
  (d) Exemplary damages under the Defend Trade Secrets Act (up to two
      times the damages award for willful and malicious misappropriation,
      18 U.S.C. § 1836(b)(3)(C));
  (e) Full attorneys' fees, litigation costs, and expert witness fees
      under 17 U.S.C. § 505 and 18 U.S.C. § 1836(b)(3)(D);
  (f) Criminal referral and prosecution where applicable under
      18 U.S.C. § 1832 (theft of trade secrets) and
      18 U.S.C. § 1030 (Computer Fraud and Abuse Act);
  (g) Disgorgement of all revenues, profits, and benefits derived from
      any unauthorized use of the Work;
  (h) Any other remedy available under applicable federal, state,
      or international law;
  (i) Technical enforcement actions including, without limitation,
      access revocation, token invalidation, and automated reporting
      through SAEIS (Article X).

The Sovereign's election not to enforce any provision in any particular
instance does not constitute a waiver of any right under this instrument,
and does not establish a course of dealing that would limit any future
enforcement.

NOTICE: SAEIS-flagged violations are automatically escalated to the
Sovereign's legal enforcement pipeline. Willful violators identified by
SAEIS are subject to enhanced damages under § 504(c)(2) and § 1836(b)(3)(C).

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ARTICLE VIII — SEVERABILITY

If any provision of this instrument is held invalid, unenforceable, or
void by any court of competent jurisdiction, that provision shall be
deemed modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable,
or severed if modification is not possible, and all remaining provisions
shall continue in full force and effect.

This instrument shall at all times be construed to provide the maximum
protection for the Sovereign's rights permitted by applicable law.

