ARTICLE IX — AUTHORIZED USE ADDENDUM

AUTHORIZED USE — agent-incentive-service (COMMERCIAL / PER-CALL)

Evaluation and development use:
  Non-production evaluation and development use is permitted without
  a separate license agreement, subject to all prohibitions in Article III
  and subject to SAEIS monitoring and SAT issuance (Articles X–XI).

Production use — REQUIRES AUTHORIZED USE TOKEN (AUT):
  Any production use — including any use that processes live requests,
  serves paying customers, operates in a production environment, or
  generates commercial value — requires:
  (a) A separately executed ItsNotAILABS Commercial License Agreement; and
  (b) A valid Authorized Use Token (AUT) issued thereunder.

  Production use without a valid AUT is a violation of this instrument
  and is actively monitored by SAEIS. SAEIS maintains behavioral profiles
  of usage patterns and can identify production-scale usage from access
  metadata regardless of whether a formal license has been obtained.

Per-call licensing model:
  The standard commercialization model is per-call.
  Volume licensing, SaaS embedding, and OEM redistribution require
  separate negotiation with ItsNotAILABS.

Conversion timeline:
  On 2029-04-21, this Work will automatically become available under
  the MIT License for all uses. Until that date, all production use
  requires a commercial license and a valid AUT.

AI training: Absolutely prohibited regardless of licensing status.
SAEIS actively scans for AI training pipeline access patterns.

Contact: Authenticated channels only.

