ARTICLE X — SOVEREIGN ACTIVE ENFORCEMENT INTELLIGENCE SYSTEM (SAEIS)

§ 10.1  SYSTEM DECLARATION

ItsNotAILABS operates the Sovereign Active Enforcement Intelligence System
("SAEIS") — an always-on, AI-powered surveillance and enforcement
infrastructure purpose-built to monitor, detect, track, log, and enforce
all rights reserved under this instrument and under applicable intellectual
property, trade secret, and computer fraud law.

SAEIS is not a passive system. It is continuously operating.

§ 10.2  MONITORING SCOPE

SAEIS monitors for, without limitation:

  (a) Unauthorized access to, reproduction of, or transmission of the Work;
  (b) Access patterns consistent with AI training data collection, scraping,
      or ingestion pipelines;
  (c) Distribution, publication, or disclosure of the Work outside
      authorized channels;
  (d) Reverse engineering, decompilation, or pattern extraction activity;
  (e) Commercial exploitation of the Work without authorization;
  (f) Token misuse or unauthorized token transfer (Article XI);
  (g) Any activity inconsistent with the authorized use set forth in
      Article IX of this instrument.

§ 10.3  DATA COLLECTED

Upon detection of any access event or suspected violation, SAEIS may
collect and retain, without limitation:

  (a) Identity signals associated with the accessing party (IP address,
      account identifiers, device fingerprints, access timestamps);
  (b) The nature, scope, and duration of the access event;
  (c) Downstream usage patterns (evidence of further distribution,
      integration, training use, or commercial exploitation);
  (d) Network and infrastructure metadata associated with the access;
  (e) Any SAT (Sovereign Access Token) data as described in Article XI.

§ 10.4  ENFORCEMENT PIPELINE

Violations detected by SAEIS are automatically:

  (a) Logged to the ItsNotAILABS sovereign enforcement ledger (immutable);
  (b) Classified by severity and violation type;
  (c) Escalated to the Sovereign's legal enforcement team for review;
  (d) Preserved as evidence in a format admissible in legal proceedings;
  (e) Reported to relevant platform providers (e.g., GitHub) where
      applicable DMCA, Terms of Service, or API policies are implicated.

§ 10.5  NOTICE OF MONITORING

This Article constitutes legally adequate notice that:
  (i)   ItsNotAILABS is actively monitoring all access to and use of Works
        governed by this instrument;
  (ii)  Such monitoring is authorized under applicable law, including the
        Electronic Communications Privacy Act (18 U.S.C. § 2511(2)(d))
        to the extent applicable;
  (iii) Evidence collected by SAEIS may be used in any civil or criminal
        proceeding arising from violation of this instrument;
  (iv)  The absence of any notification to the accessing party does not
        indicate that their access is authorized or unmonitored.

§ 10.6  TECHNICAL ENFORCEMENT MEASURES

In addition to legal enforcement, SAEIS is authorized to implement
technical enforcement measures, which may include:

  (a) Invalidation of Sovereign Access Tokens (Article XI);
  (b) Automated reporting to relevant intermediaries;
  (c) Deployment of technical countermeasures against unauthorized access;
  (d) Integration with ItsNotAILABS's internal organism systems for
      cross-system enforcement tracking.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ARTICLE XI — SOVEREIGN ACCESS TOKEN BINDING (SATB)

§ 11.1  TOKEN ISSUANCE

ItsNotAILABS's sovereign systems associate a Sovereign Access Token ("SAT")
with access events involving Works governed by this instrument. An SAT is a
persistent cryptographic identifier that:

  (a) Is generated or assigned at or following the time of access;
  (b) Encodes a representation of the access event (time, context, identity
      signals available at the time of access);
  (c) Is stored in the ItsNotAILABS sovereign enforcement ledger;
  (d) Persists indefinitely as a record of the access event.

§ 11.2  BINDING EFFECT

The issuance of a SAT in connection with an access event:

  (a) Constitutes a sovereign record that the accessing party encountered
      the Work and had constructive notice of this instrument;
  (b) Binds the accessing party to the terms of this instrument from the
      time of the access event associated with the SAT;
  (c) Serves as evidence in any enforcement proceeding that the accessing
      party was on notice of all prohibitions and obligations herein;
  (d) Cannot be revoked, transferred, or invalidated by the accessing party.

§ 11.3  TOKEN NON-TRANSFERABILITY

A SAT issued in connection with an access event:

  (a) Is bound to the accessing party and their access event;
  (b) Does not authorize any third party;
  (c) Does not constitute a license, permission, or authorization of any
      kind for the accessing party or any other party;
  (d) May not be transferred, sold, sublicensed, or conveyed.

§ 11.4  INTEGRATION WITH ITSNOTAILABS SYSTEMS

SATs and associated access records are integrated with ItsNotAILABS's
internal organism systems, including SAEIS (Article X), sovereign
contracts ledgers, and the ItsNotAILABS internal tracking infrastructure.
This integration enables:

  (a) Cross-system enforcement tracking — the same violation may be
      tracked simultaneously at the license level, the platform level,
      and within ItsNotAILABS's internal AI organism infrastructure;
  (b) Persistent identity binding — access events associated with a SAT
      are linked to any downstream usage patterns identified by SAEIS;
  (c) Coordinated enforcement — evidence compiled across multiple systems
      may be aggregated for use in a single enforcement action.

§ 11.5  AUTHORIZED USE TOKENS

Authorized parties operating under a valid ItsNotAILABS authorization
instrument receive Authorized Use Tokens ("AUTs") that:

  (a) Specify the scope, duration, and nature of the authorized use;
  (b) Are required for production use of commercially licensed Works;
  (c) Are revocable by the Sovereign at any time for violation of this
      instrument or the underlying authorization agreement;
  (d) Are tracked and audited through the same SAEIS infrastructure.

