ARTICLE XII — LIVING INSTRUMENT DECLARATION

§ 12.1  CONTINUOUS OPERATION

This instrument is a living enforcement document. It is continuously
active and continuously enforced. The obligations it creates do not
lapse, expire, or diminish through inaction, delay, or the passage of
time, except as specifically provided herein.

§ 12.2  INSTRUMENT UPDATES

The Sovereign may update, revise, or extend this instrument at any time.
Updated versions carry a new version number in the Instrument Reference
and are published at the Sovereign's authorized channels. The most
recent published version governs all new access events from its effective
date. Prior versions continue to govern access events that occurred under
those versions.

§ 12.3  AI-ENFORCED CONTINUITY

ItsNotAILABS's AI systems (SAEIS and related organism infrastructure)
operate continuously and without interruption. The temporary unavailability
of any technical enforcement component does not suspend the legal
obligations created by this instrument, does not constitute a waiver of
any right, and does not authorize any otherwise-prohibited conduct.

§ 12.4  ENTERPRISE ACKNOWLEDGMENT

This instrument is drafted to enterprise-grade IP standards. It creates
obligations enforceable against individuals, corporations, partnerships,
LLCs, trusts, non-profit organizations, government contractors, and all
other legal entities without distinction. The Sovereign has retained and
consulted with qualified intellectual property counsel in the design of
this enforcement framework.

§ 12.5  CROSS-JURISDICTIONAL ENFORCEMENT

The Sovereign's enforcement rights under this instrument extend to all
jurisdictions in which the Work has been accessed, reproduced, distributed,
or exploited. The Sovereign may enforce this instrument in any jurisdiction
in which a court of competent jurisdiction may exercise authority over the
violating party or the violating conduct. The choice of Texas law in this
instrument does not limit the Sovereign's enforcement rights in other
jurisdictions.

